# (#8346) The harness result ledger no longer lives in a single appended file,
# so the `merge=union` rule that used to be here is GONE rather than retargeted.
#
# It was `/test/results/ledger.jsonl merge=union`, with a long rationale for why
# union was safe for JSONL. The rule is unnecessary under one file per run --
# two writers never touch the same path, so there is nothing to merge -- and
# leaving it would be worse than unnecessary: this repo's .git/config shadowed
# git's BUILT-IN union driver with a no-op `true` for months (#8348), so every
# `merge=union` path silently resolved to "ours" and three real gate records
# were lost. A rule whose driver can be disarmed from a file nobody reads is not
# a mechanism you want in the path of a data file.
#
# The completeness guard (#8349, `ledger_compare.py --lint-merge`) is what
# actually holds the property now, and it is mechanism-independent by design: it
# asserts the merge result retains every run_id from either parent and never
# asks WHY one vanished, so it survives a layout change and a driver regression
# alike.
